# armour/man/tabard: the watch's tabard over the man's mail (P2c slice, SLICE-ARMOUR; STYLE_P2 25.2 "cloth over mail"):
# cloth in the accent slot (tabardColor) on the chest plane, lit like A3's tunic (a lit plane, the shadow side, one fold under
# the belt, a solid lit hem), its side edges a step-0 line against the mail, its hem two rows above the mail skirt's hem in
# every view (rest: y-8 over the mail's y-6; the side walk and run: y-10 over the mail and its hang at y-8). The belt cinches
# it. The kingdom's device (Device slot, 5 px, centred on the chest) is the `when device` region. The mail shows at the
# shoulders, on the arms and below the hem. The mail's glint (one step-4 pixel on the lit shoulder facing down and up, on the collar facing right and left) rides the
# bob. Laid down (the L lie) the skirt flap folds under: the
# mail shows between the belt and the shield on the corpse (i3: the panel read tabard and shield as one red box). The run (`runl`) keeps the hem a pixel FORWARD of the method's lean rows, so it
# kicks out while the mail skirt trails. Keys: rest idle run runl drawn swing lie in D U R L. Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
use person
body man
role overlay tabard
layer torso
anchor neck
keys torso
z 3
legend D device 2
legend Q device 3
legend H device 1

